{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he saw the place from afar.</b> They said in the Midrash: Abraham said to Isaac, 'Do you see what I see?' He said to him, 'I see a fine and praiseworthy mountain, with a cloud bound upon it.' He said to the servants, 'Do you see anything?' They said to him, 'We see nothing but wildernesses and mountains.' He said to them, 'Stay here with the donkey — with one who is like a donkey: just as the donkey does not see, so you do not see.' 'Stay here, and I and the lad will go thus far.' What will be in the end, when the Holy One, blessed be He, said to me, 'Thus shall your seed be'? He was thirty-seven years old, and Scripture calls him 'lad.' But this is the way of Scriptures in such matters, and likewise we find concerning Joshua, as it is written (Exodus 33:11): ״ומשרתו יהושע בן נון נער לא ימיש״ — and he was fifty-six years old."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:03.581088721Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}